ven-names>DI</given-names></name><name><surname>Trivedi</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name><name><surname>Barlow</surname><given-names>CE</given-names></name><name><surname>Dunn</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><name><surname>Kampert</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Inverse association between physical inactivity and mental health in men and women</article-title><source>Medicine and Science in Sport and Exercise</source><year>2006</year><volume>38</volume><fpage>173</fpage><lpage>178</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1249/01.mss.0000180883.32116.28</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ford</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name><name><surname>Burton</surname><given-names>NW</given-names></name><name><surname>Marshall</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><name><surname>Dobson</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Prospective study of physical activity and depressive symptoms in middle-aged women</article-title><source>American Journal of Preventive Medicine</source><year>2005</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>265</fpage><lpage>272</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16242588</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.amepre.2005.06.009</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Harris</surname><given-names>AHS</given-names></name><name><surname>Cronkite</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Moos</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Physical activity, exercise coping, and depression in a 10-year cohort study of depressed patients</article-title><source>Journal of Affective Disorders</source><year>2006</year><volume>93</volume><fpage>79</fpage><lpage>85</lpage><