Scandinavian Journal of Medicine and Science in Sports</source><year>2002</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>241</fpage><lpage>247</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12199874</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1034/j.1600-0838.2002.00341.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Mishra</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Bauman</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Leisure time physical activity in Australian women: Relationship with well being and symptoms</article-title><source>Research Quarterly for Exercise and Sport</source><year>2000</year><volume>71</volume><fpage>206</fpage><lpage>216</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10999258</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Singh</surname><given-names>NA</given-names></name><name><surname>Clements</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Fiatarone</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A randomized controlled trial of progressive resistance training in depressed elders</article-title><source>J Gerontol A Biol Sci Med Sci</source><year>1997</year><volume>52A</volume><fpage>M27</fpage><lpage>M35</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9008666</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Norvell</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Martin</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Salamon</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Psychological and physiological benefits of passive and aerobic exercise in sedentary middle-aged women</article-title><source>The Jour